# DDD core

## Dependency direction

- **Domain** (pure TypeScript): entities, value objects, domain services, invariants. No Vue, Nuxt, Nitro, Prisma, or HTTP imports.
- **Application**: **use-case classes** (PascalCase, e.g. `ListPublicCompetitions`, `FindUserById`) in `application/<context>/`; constructor-inject **ports** (`export interface` in `application/ports/`—repository contracts, mail, clocks). Keep them **stateless** (no mutable fields beyond injected ports). Thin **public** methods orchestrate ports and domain types only—no `.vue` files.
- **Infrastructure**: **implements** ports (e.g. repository **classes** in `infrastructure/persistence/` with `implements SomeRepository`). Inject dependencies (Prisma client, adapters) via constructors. May import Prisma and framework adapters here only.
- **Presentation / delivery**: `app/**` and thin `server/api/**` handlers—map HTTP ↔ use cases; no business rules duplicated ad hoc in templates.

Allowed flow: `presentation → application → domain`; `infrastructure` implements ports consumed by application. **Domain never depends on infrastructure or UI.**

## Bounded contexts (organise by folder namespaces)

Use separate slices (e.g. per context: `domain`, `application`, `infrastructure`) rather than one flat `models` tree. Prefer **singular** names for party-style contexts (`user`, `archer`) and **plural** for catalog/event-style contexts (`competitions`, `participations`).

- **user** — accounts, sessions, roles, invitations (when present).
- **archer** — internal Archer records and optional linkage to a user account.
- **competitions** — competition events (metadata, lifecycle).
- **participations** — participation records (Archer ↔ Competition), including **fee status** per participation.
- **website** — public site content and JSON `website_config` (site settings, opening hours, tarifs, text sections, gallery).
- **file** — stored files and related metadata (e.g. competition documents; not the landing-gallery CDN flow).

Cross-context calls go through application-layer orchestration or explicit anti-corruption layers—avoid “god” imports across contexts.

## Use-case naming

- One class per user-visible or system action; **PascalCase** imperative name (verb + object), e.g. `InviteMember`, `RecordParticipationPayment`.
- File name: **`kebab-case.use-case.ts`** (e.g. `list-public-competitions.use-case.ts`). Rely on path + suffix for “use case”; do not repeat a `UseCase` suffix on the class unless disambiguation is needed.

## Shared kernel

Put **DTOs and types** shared by client and server under `shared/` (or equivalent). Keep them free of framework imports where possible.

## Nuxt path aliases (imports)

In this repo, **`~` resolves to the Nuxt `app/` directory**. Import code **outside** `app/` (e.g. `domain/`, `application/`, `infrastructure/`, `shared/`) using the **project root** alias **`~~/`** (e.g. `~~/domain/...`, `~~/application/...`). Use `~/` for assets and files under `app/` only. Wrong: `~/domain/...` (would resolve under `app/`).

## Composition root (repositories)

Server and other composition roots obtain repository **instances** from **`infrastructure/persistence/repositories.provider.ts`** (or a renamed successor). Do not import concrete repository modules from `server/` except through that provider—see `.cursor/rules/prisma-repository.mdc` and `biome.json`.
